~ day_start
Kid: Mum... are we there yet?
Mum: [color=firebrick]What?![/color] We've only just started!
Kid: Long car rides are so [shake]borrring[/shake].
Mum: This is going to be a long [color=firebrick]3 day road trip[/color], and it looks like this weather's going to be with us for a while...
Kid: Ooh, I could pass the time by [color=goldenrod]racing raindrops[/color]!
Mum: That sounds fun!


do game.play_cutscene(1, "tutorial")

=> END


~ tutorial

do game.next_overlay()

Kid: I wonder which of those [wave][color=steel_blue]raindrops[/color][/wave] will reach the bottom first...

# ADD A WAY TO SHOW THE FIRST SPAWNED RAINDROP'S BUBBLE
Kid: If I hover my mouse over them, I can see their [color=steel_blue]stats[/color]! 
Kid: [color=goldenrod]Weight[/color] affects their top speed, [color=goldenrod]acceleration[/color] changes how fast they pick up speed, and [color=goldenrod]magnetism[/color] affects how long they stay in a water streak for!
Kid: Once I've made my choice, I can [color=steel_blue]click[/color] on the raindrop to select it, and then hit [color=forest_green]Go![/color]
do game.next_overlay()
do raise_dialogue_box()
Kid: Depending on where my raindrop finishes, I can get lots of [color=goldenrod]points.[/color]
do game.next_overlay()
do lower_dialogue_box()
Kid: And I can see how much [color=goldenrod]time[/color] I've got left of the day up here.
do game.next_overlay()
Kid: Let's get [color=forest_green]racing![/color]

do game.begin_game()

=> END

~ day_end
Mum: Oh look, the [color=goldenrod]sun[/color] is out!
Kid: Are we there yet?
Mum: Not even close.

do game.end_day()

=> END